\ A self-recursive word compiled at definition time. The self-call resolves while the body is
\ compiling, which mints the word's id and bakes it into the code. The code has to be installed
\ under that same id, or every other level of the recursion finds no code and falls back through
\ the interpreter. The trace shows one compile and a dispatch hit only at the outer call, since
\ every level below it is a direct compiled call.

deep: stack-recursive ( n -- n ) [ dup 0 > [ 1 - deep 1 + ] [ ] if ] ;

10 deep .
